# Amendment cycle — namespaced-labels-and-bootout (#6, 2026-04-22,
# sixth amendment): amendment #5 landed a clean detached first-run
# but a real-world fresh-clone install (Luke's pos3 workspace) still
# halted at phase-4b-health-poll with `service-health-timeout:com.
# pos.orchestrator`. Root cause: ServiceManagerRunner.bootstrap called
# `launchctl bootstrap gui/<uid> <plist>` without first issuing a
# `launchctl bootout gui/<uid>/<label>` — launchd treats bootstrap as
# a no-op when the label is already loaded, so any cached path from a
# prior install (the test-harness tempdir in Luke's case) survives
# across the scaffold's plist rewrite. Additional defect: service
# labels were hard-coded (`com.pos.orchestrator`, `com.pos-v2.memory-
