2026-04-25. Closes the first-run primary-persona-default-agent-
wiring family per master plan `docs/rebuild/plans/first-run-
primary-persona-default-agent-wiring.md` and sub-plan
`docs/rebuild/plans/amendment-37-hands-off-lifecycle-default-
agent-wiring.md`. Predecessor amendments #35 (primary-persona
renderer + onboarding + is_starter) sealed at ce07242; #36
(workspace-bootstrap persona-scaffold) sealed at 0031d1e.

The amendment lands two new responsibilities on the existing
first-run hook surface inside the hands-off-lifecycle fence:

  - `hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_settings.py` —
    `merge_session_start(...)` gains an optional `agent_handle:
    str | None = None` parameter. When provided, the merger
    sets `existing["agent"] = agent_handle` after the
    SessionStart-stanza merge so a fresh Claude Code session
    selects the workspace persona as its default subagent.
    The pre-amendment-#37 callers (no agent_handle) are
    backwards-compatible — the field is left untouched.

  - `hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/agent_file_authoring.py` (new) —
    stdlib-only writer for `<workspace>/.claude/agents/
    <handle>.md`. Atomic write via `.tmp` sibling +
    `os.replace`; write-only-if-different policy preserves
    mtime stability across re-runs (AC37.3). Failures are
    returned via `AgentFileWriteResult` rather than raising —
    the caller's graceful-degradation path inspects the
    dataclass and routes the diagnostic.

  - `hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/agent_file_runner.py` (new) —
    thin CLI runner that spawns under the shared venv. Loads
    the workspace persona via `PersonaLoader.primary()`, calls
    `to_agent_md(loaded.contract, prompt_text=loaded.prompt_
    text)`, and emits a JSON envelope `{"handle": "<handle>",
    "body": "<rendered>"}` on stdout. Mirrors the established
    `first_run_scaffold_runner.py` pattern — the helper itself
    stays stdlib-only.

  - `hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_helper.py` — new
    Phase 4c (agent-file authorship) inserted between Phase 4a
    (scaffold) and Phase 4b (health poll). Spawns the runner,
    parses the envelope, writes the agent file, then re-merges
    settings.json with `agent_handle=<resolved>`. Phase 6
    self-retire threads `agent_handle` through so the post-
    retire settings.json carries the agent field. Every
    failure path (subprocess timeout, JSON parse error, runner
    non-zero exit, write-permission denied) is caught and
    surfaced via `_advance_state` — the helper never halts on
    this phase.

Behaviour:

  - On a fresh-clone first-run, after the workspace-bootstrap
    scaffold (amendment #36) materialises `<workspace>/personas/
    <handle>/`, Phase 4c renders `.claude/agents/<handle>.md`
    from the contract via amendment #35's `to_agent_md()` and
    merges `"agent": "<handle>"` into `.claude/settings.json`.
  - Subsequent SessionStart hooks re-load the agent file as
    Claude Code's structural identity-anchor; the context-load
    gate (amendment #32) still composes `additionalContext`
    with the runtime persona context.
  - Re-running first-run on a workspace whose persona contract
    is non-starter is a no-op for the agent file (write-only-
    if-different) and preserves the settings.json `"agent"`
    field. User edits to the contract reach the agent file via
    the persona-layer reload path, not via the first-run path.
  - Agent-file write failure (permissions, malformed
    settings.json that cannot merge) surfaces a structured
    diagnostic via `_advance_state` and proceeds; the
    SessionStart hook still fires; the gate still loads; the
    session degrades to generic-Claude-with-context-load-gate.

No source edits to primary-persona/, workspace-bootstrap/, or
any other sealed component. The agent renderer is consumed by
importing it inside the runner subprocess; the scaffolded
persona directory is consumed by reading it from disk in the
same subprocess.

